## Goal
Surface the game compiler's string-by-reference sanity-check warning for parity.

## Source
todo-cover-cases-next.txt — Case 3 (2026-04-20, tm-control-mcp)

## Compiler (game-side)
`MCP: Sanity check: Use 'const string &in x' to pass a string by reference`

## Acceptance
- [ ] Function params typed as bare `string` (by value) emit a warning suggesting `const string &in`
- [ ] Params already `const string &in` / `string &in` are silent
- [ ] Warning severity (not error) so it does not fail check exit codes unless configured

## Notes
Nice-to-have parity so iteration avoids extra game-compile cycles. Lower priority than real type errors.